cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or its experimental data, please cite Kunlunxin-FFT; cite cuButterfly for the hybrid dataflow method."
title: "Kunlunxin-FFT: A Hardware-Mapped FFT Operator Library for Kunlunxin P800"
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: "Teng"
    family-names: "Wang"
    email: "wangt635@ustc.edu.cn"
    affiliation: "High Efficient Intelligent Computing Lab, Suzhou Institute for Advanced Research, University of Science and Technology of China, Suzhou, China"
repository-code: "https://github.com/TruNcat3/kunlunxin-fft"
url: "https://truncat3.github.io/kunlunxin-fft/"
abstract: >-
  An FFT operator library and reproducible research artifact for Kunlunxin
  P800. It migrates the cuButterfly hybrid spatial-temporal dataflow method
  to the Triton-XMLIR-XPU device path, separates architecture mapping from
  processing-unit selection and hardware lowering, and provides M0-M5
  implementations, a profile-bound frozen selector, conservative fallback,
  batched execution, correctness gates, and a traceable release matrix.
  The current verified interface covers fp32 complex forward C2C transforms
  at power-of-two lengths up to 1048576 on the recorded P800 stack.
keywords:
  - FFT
  - Kunlunxin
  - P800
  - Triton
  - XMLIR
  - XPU
  - butterfly
  - hybrid-dataflow
license: Apache-2.0
